          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">HKT times from 00:00 to 12:59 PM belong to the previous calendar day in EST. Always verify the date.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Assuming 12-Hour Shift Instead of 13</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">The difference between UTC+8 and UTC-5 is 13 hours, not 12. Using 12 hours causes a 1-hour scheduling error.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Confusing EST with EDT</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">EST is UTC-5 (winter). EDT is UTC-4 (summer). Using EST during summer introduces a 1-hour shift relative to New York local clocks.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

